-- title:
--   Finite program for the fixed projected subgradient solver
-- statement:
--   This is the fixed 237-instruction solver program. Inputs are the finite arrays $a_i,c_i$ and $\eta$; the output array contains the earliest best iterate and integer memory records its index. It counts upward to
--
--   $$T=\lceil4/\eta^2\rceil$$
--
--   using comparisons, evaluates every residual, chooses the earliest maximizing index, applies the explicit radial projected update, and keeps the earliest strict improvement. No optimizer, ceiling or real-to-integer primitive occurs. The program returns a computed vector; its norm, residual, agreement with the mathematical iterates and resource bounds are theorem conclusions.
-- source:
--   Vladimir Braverman, Kuan Cheng, Jiaqing Zhu, STOC 2027 submission #1373 (October 2026), pp. 18–20, Lemma 5.2, equation (36) and the return rule on p.20; https://github.com/sigact-stoc/stoc2027/releases/download/papers-2/1373.pdf

